  "body": "## What fails\n\nThe batch tier of the post-merge gate fails in step 1, `debug build (--no-run)`, with exit 101.\n\n- Run 43935486746 on c3c9f9a3a (merge of PR #2101).\n- Run 43935744100 on 545a88e34 (tip at that time).\n\nThe public log shows no compiler error, because the gate writes the cargo output to its step log only. A local build of the same command on origin/main e3f7d122b gives this error:\n\n```\ncrates\\app\\tests\\wire_tool.rs:107:19: error[E0308]: mismatched types: expected `Option<WorkMaterial>`, found `WorkMaterial`\ncrates\\app\\tests\\wire_tool.rs:106:15: error[E0063]: missing fields `stepdown` and `stepover` in initializer of `CuttingRow`: missing `stepdown` and `stepover`\nerror: could not compile `camcraft-app` (test \"wire_tool\") due to 2 previous errors\n```\n\n## Cause\n\nTwo PRs built alone, but they clash after the merge:\n\n- PR #2140 (merge 1b6e08182, #2011 EDM wire tool) added the test `wire_tool_command_refuses_bad_rpm_diameter_corner_and_cutting_rows_by_name`. It builds a `CuttingRow` literal with `material: WorkMaterial` and no step fields.\n- PR #2101 (merge c3c9f9a3a, it includes the #2015 Unknown cutting row) changed `CuttingRow`. `material` is now `Option<WorkMaterial>`, and the struct has the new fields `stepdown` and `stepover`.\n\nOnly test code fails. Product code builds. The xtask gate change of #1952 is not the cause.\n\n## Done means\n\n- `wire_tool.rs` builds the row with `CuttingRow::plain(Some(WorkMaterial::MildSteel), 0.0, 50.0)`. The test keeps its assertion: a wire tool with a cutting row is refused with \"EDM conditions\".\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-kernel -p camcraft-cl -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --no-run` builds.\n- The `wire_tool` test binary passes.\n",
